As a minor practical suggestion, I note that starting from the logicl form =
and working back to the phonological realization is, in one repect easier t=
han 'tother way 'round, since you have a certainty for a start. =C2=A0Of co=
urse, you then have a variety of ways that things can go, since one form gi=
ves rise to a large number of different phonological strings. =C2=A0But =C2=
=A0each difference is achieved (ideally) in a unique way and a suitable gra=
mmar will require marks for exactly those unique steps and no others, for a=
 significant net savings compared to the present systems (it seems to me, w=
ho am often annoyed by what seem to be irrelevant requirements put in becau=
se they ae useful somewhere sometime).=20

